# Important-gate registry (plan 04-24, D-46, RUN-04), checked by the gate step important-gates.
# An important gate is one whose silent pass would let a requirement, claim or evidence tier be
# asserted without evidence: it is the sole evidence for a requirement or claim, it can pass
# vacuously (inventory, digest or golden comparison, outcome classifier, refusal/no-state-change
# check, verdict over producer output), or its failure class escaped once.
# Columns: <gate> <fault|control|mutant> <id> <REQ>. A fault is judged by faults-verdict (must-fail
# vector, allowed reason prefixes, must-pass vector); a control by tools/check/run-controls.sh
# (EXPECT token); a mutant is an in-step selftest case (pkg-selftests.ids, ci-summary-selftests.ids)
# or a suite self-control `<suite>.judge.<slug>` / `<suite>.mutant.<slug>` that passes only when
# its check fails for the intended reason. The audit behind this list is in
# .planning/phases/04-headless-runner-and-installed-consumer/04-24-SUMMARY.md.
# Phase 5 (plan 05-12) extends the registry to INP-01 INP-02 INP-03 API-03 AUD-01 AUD-02 (section below the Phase 4 lines).

# API-02: absolute run bound, overshoot reported, slicing invariance (suite run, runner slicing),
# timebase growth of ivs_info, pinned stop reasons.
run-bound fault RUN_TARGET_UNCHECKED API-02
run-bound fault RUN_STOP_BEFORE_OVERSHOOT API-02
run-bound fault RUN_FAULT_STEPS API-02
run-slice fault RUN_BUDGET_CARRY API-02
run-info fault INFO_TAIL_UNGUARDED API-02
runner-time fault RUNNER_SLICE_DROPS_REMAINDER API-02
api-define-pins control api-stop-unpinned API-02
api-define-pins control api-stop-renumbered API-02
api-define-pins control api-stop-orphan API-02

# API-04: caller-owned output buffers refused before any state change; pinned refusal reasons.
output-buffers fault RUN_CAPACITY_AFTER_STEP API-04
output-buffers fault OUTBUF_PARTIAL_WRITE API-04
api-define-pins control api-reason-unpinned API-04

