# SCN-01 (plan 07-02, A-13): the oracle checks of the first visible original program. A declared frame pair whose planes differ outside its rectangle, and a progress predicate (tier playable-guest-progress) without an input line or without progress, are refused. Later plans append the mutant, judge and consumer lines.
scn-video-pair control video-frame-pair-region-drift SCN-01
scn-shape control golden-shape-no-input SCN-01
scn-shape control golden-shape-no-progress SCN-01
# SCN-01 (plan 07-07, T-07-17): the metamorphic judge. A pass run whose video digest equals the idle run's (the response is not in the frames), a scenario whose scripted input was not consumed (events after the last bound or ignored), and an idle run that is audible are each refused by the pair judge; each self-control passes only when the judge rejects its fake report pair for that reason.
scn-differential mutant runner-process.judge.pair-video-equal SCN-01
scn-differential mutant runner-process.judge.input-not-consumed SCN-01
scn-differential mutant runner-process.judge.idle-audible SCN-01
# SCN-01 (plan 07-08, D-25, D-10, A-14, A-17): the program mutants of the Lamp Tone program, one per failure class of the derivation table (g): the input decode, the progress store, the lamp complement, the amplitude value, the ungated sound (judged under the idle scenario), both re-arm edges, the late strobe, the missing EIS, the halt in the idle branch and the two stub-vector mutants (JD as J, the interrupt target tie). Each ends with its stated first failing clause and, on the channel-isolation rows, its complete failing set (the fails column). The negative row (re-arm inside the band) must still pass and is not a registry line.
scn-mutants mutant runner-process.mutant.SCN-INPUT-PORT SCN-01
scn-mutants mutant runner-process.mutant.SCN-PROGRESS-STORE SCN-01
scn-mutants mutant runner-process.mutant.SCN-LAMP-COMPLEMENT SCN-01
scn-mutants mutant runner-process.mutant.SCN-AMP-VALUE SCN-01
scn-mutants mutant runner-process.mutant.SCN-SOUND-UNGATED SCN-01
scn-mutants mutant runner-process.mutant.SCN-REARM-SHORT SCN-01
scn-mutants mutant runner-process.mutant.SCN-REARM-LONG SCN-01
scn-mutants mutant runner-process.mutant.SCN-STROBE-LATE SCN-01
scn-mutants mutant runner-process.mutant.SCN-NO-EIS SCN-01
scn-mutants mutant runner-process.mutant.SCN-HLT-IDLE SCN-01
scn-mutants mutant runner-process.mutant.SCN-STUB-JD-AS-J SCN-01
scn-mutants mutant runner-process.mutant.SCN-ISR-TIE SCN-01
# SCN-01 (plan 07-09, D-26, T-07-21): the installed-consumer replay of the pass scenario. The consumer's scn.digest lines and observed domains are compared with the runner golden of demo-lamp-tone-pass; a consumer that never read the audio samples (a dropped scn.digest.audio line) and a consumer whose video digest differs from the runner's (a changed scn.digest.video nibble) are each refused by the pkg-install step.
pkg-install mutant scn-domain-missing SCN-01
pkg-install mutant scn-digest-drift SCN-01
